<title>HUNGARY: Hungary six-month bill yield falls to 22.59 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary six-month bill yield falls to 22.59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of six-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.59 percent, down from 22.62 percent at an auction two weeks ago, Government Debt Management Centre said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow, and on  HTBO.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     14,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	25,284.27 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    12,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 13,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.59 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     89.9263 pct</p>
</text>
